        "thinking": "The issue is clear. The server's `GetObjectResult.stream` is typed as `Readable` (Node.js stream), while the CF package's `GetObjectResult.stream` is typed as `ReadableStream` (Web Streams API). Since `R2Provider` returns a Web `ReadableStream`, it's not assignable to the server's `StorageProviderFactory` which expects `StorageProviderImpl` where `getObject` returns a `Readable`.\n\nThe boot.ts error at line 61 is:\n```ts\nregisterStorageProvider(\"r2\", (_config) =\u003e {\n\n\n```\n\nAnd `registerStorageProvider` expects `factory: (config: Config) =\u003e StorageProviderImpl` where `StorageProviderImpl` requires `stream: Readable`.\n\nThe simplest fix here that doesn't break the server types is to cast `R2Provider as unknown as StorageProviderImpl` in the boot registration, since at runtime the Worker will use Web Streams, not Node Streams. I'm returning a new R2Provider instance with the bucket configuration, but I need to verify what `StorageProviderImpl` actually requires in the provider-registry to make sure this cast is safe.\n\n```",
        "type": "thinking"
      }
